To make this completely plug-and-play across all your tools, I just added a universal `N8nIntegrationEngine` directly into your `@USER/shared-kawaii-ui` workspace! 

Here is how beautifully simple this makes things for your plugin devs. Any plugin inside `anymd` or `mbb` can now just do this:

```typescript
import { n8nEngine } from '@USER/shared-kawaii-ui';

// 1. Fire and forget (e.g., Save this markdown to Dropbox)
n8nEngine.fireAndForget('save-to-dropbox-webhook-id', {
  filename: 'my-note.md',
  content: '# Hello World'
});

// 2. Fetch data (e.g., Get what's currently playing on Spotify)
const trackData = await n8nEngine.triggerWorkflow('get-spotify-track-id', {}, true);
console.log(trackData.title);
```

By abstracting it into the shared UI package, you've created a universal API gateway. Whenever you want to add a new service (Notion, Google Docs, Spotify), you just drag-and-drop the nodes in n8n's visual builder, expose a Webhook URL, and use `n8nEngine` in your code to talk to it. 

No more dealing with SSL certificates, OAuth redirect URIs, or managing dozens of API keys inside your front-end code! Should we look into replacing some of the manual Google/IFTTT webhook logic in `mbb` with this new engine, or are you ready to test out the new Dual-Pane UI first?

